# Agent review pipeline

After **implementing features**, **refactors**, or **bugfixes**, run reviews before claiming work is complete.

## Automatic triggers

| Situation | Agents (parallel when possible) |
|-----------|----------------------------------|
| Feature or bugfix done | `code-reviewer`, `security-reviewer`, `clean-code-reviewer` |
| Auth, OAuth, Keycloak, CORS, admin API | also `security-reviewer` (mandatory) |
| New endpoints, service split, Docker | also `architecture-reviewer` |
| Dependency or config change | `best-practices-reviewer` |
| User asks "how does X work" / onboarding | `project-context` |
| Before commit / PR / "done" | `verifier` |

## Invocation

- Delegate via Task/subagent: `/code-reviewer`, `/security-reviewer`, etc.
- Or: "Use the security-reviewer subagent on these changes"
- Run independent reviewers **in parallel**; run `verifier` **last** after fixes.

## Playbook files

Detailed prompts: `.cursor/agents/*.md`

## Fix policy

Reviewers are **readonly** except `verifier`. Apply Critical/High security and correctness findings before marking complete. Summarize review results in a compact table for the user.
